@startuml draft-checkpoint-lifecycle
' Lifecycle of a DraftBuffer with checkpoint / undo for editor-style completion.
' A draft is the term being typed at the cursor; checkpoint() pushes a lightweight
' snapshot (the buffer length) onto the CheckpointStack, and undo() pops the most
' recent snapshot and truncates the buffer back to it. commit() finalizes the
' draft; reset() clears everything back to Empty.
' Color: contextual completion (deep purple #EDE7F6 / #4527A0); the undo edges are
'   drawn in deletion-red #C62828 because undo discards just-typed characters.
'   src/contextual/draft_buffer.rs · src/contextual/checkpoint.rs
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
hide empty description
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor #EDE7F6
  BorderColor #4527A0
  FontColor #102027
}
skinparam ArrowColor #4527A0
skinparam ArrowThickness 2

title DraftBuffer lifecycle — checkpoint / undo over the term being typed

[*] --> Empty

Empty        --> Editing      : insert(c) / delete()
Editing      --> Editing      : insert(c) / delete()
Editing      --> Checkpointed : checkpoint():\npush length to CheckpointStack
Checkpointed --> Editing      : insert(c) / delete()\n(continue editing)

' undo() pops the most recent checkpoint and truncates the buffer (red = discards input)
Editing      -[#C62828]->     Editing : undo(): pop checkpoint
Checkpointed -[#C62828]->     Editing : undo(): pop checkpoint

Editing      --> Committed    : commit()
Committed    --> [*]

' reset() returns to Empty from any active state
Editing      --> Empty        : reset()
Checkpointed --> Empty        : reset()
Committed    --> Empty        : reset()
@enduml
